course: dictionary
lesson: 6768
title: Opium
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Opium is a noun. It is a strong, illegal drug made from the juice of a kind of poppy. Opium is uncountable, so you say some opium, not an opium. «Then Britain kept selling opium, a harmful drug, into China.» The words harmful drug tell you that opium is bad for people.
explain: Opium makes people sleepy, and it is very addictive. Addictive means people find it very hard to stop taking it, even when they know it is hurting them. That is why it is dangerous.
explain: Doctors sometimes use medicines made from opium, such as morphine, to stop very bad pain. Only doctors should give these strong painkillers. Opium the illegal drug and opium-based medicine are not the same thing, so always ask who gave it and why.
explain: Opium is part of a famous piece of history. «In 1839 Commissioner Lin Zexu had more than a thousand tonnes of British opium destroyed.» Then Britain went to war. Read the sentences around the word, and you can see that the Opium Wars were about this drug.
fact: Opium is a strong, illegal drug made from the juice of a kind of poppy.
fact: Opium makes people sleepy and is very addictive and dangerous.
fact: Medicines made from opium, like morphine, are used by doctors to stop very bad pain.
fact: The Opium War of 1839–1842 ended with Hong Kong going to Britain.
fact: Opium is uncountable: you say some opium, not an opium.
exercise: «Britain sold the harmful drug opium in China.» What kind of drug is opium? | Tasty sweets | *A dangerous drug | A kind of tea | A cold medicine for children
exercise: Opium is called addictive. What does addictive mean? | Easy to share with friends | Sold in a shop next to the tea | *Very hard to stop taking | Tasty and sweet
exercise: «In 1839 Commissioner Lin Zexu had more than a thousand tonnes of British opium destroyed.» Find and copy one word that means got rid of completely. | *destroyed | tonnes | British | Commissioner
test: Doctors use medicines made from opium, such as morphine, for what purpose? | To keep people awake all night | To cure a cold in one day | *To stop very bad pain | To make people run faster
test: Which two countries fought the First Opium War of 1839–1842? | *Britain and China | China and Japan | Britain and Germany | Britain and Russia
exam: Why did China ban opium? | Because doctors gave it to every child | *Because it is harmful and addictive | Because it tasted awful and nobody bought it | Because it was too cheap to sell
